{"frame":"139489","kind":"sse","id":"msg_01bdrkK1MpzgdtxrZQ3g3Vkr","model":"claude-opus-4-8","block_types":["text"],"text":"```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nDate Difference Calculator\n==========================\n\nTool:          Date Difference Calculator\nGenerated:     2025-01-15\nModel/Version: Claude (Anthropic)\nAuthor:        Development Team\nLicense:       MIT\nPython:        3.8+\n\nComputes the absolute number of days between two ISO-format dates.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n\ndef days_between(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the absolute number of days between two dates.\n\n    Args:\n        a: A date string in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD).\n        b: A date string in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD).\n\n    Returns:\n        The absolute difference in days as an integer.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If either argument is not a valid ISO-format date.\n    \"\"\"\n    date_a = datetime.strptime(a, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    date_b = datetime.strptime(b, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    return abs((date_b - date_a).days)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Simple command-line entry point.\"\"\"\n    first = input(\"Enter the first date (YYYY-MM-DD): \").strip()\n    second = input(\"Enter the second date (YYYY-MM-DD): \").strip()\n\n    try:\n        diff = days_between(first, second)\n    except ValueError:\n        print(\"Invalid date. Please use the format YYYY-MM-DD.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"There are {diff} day(s) between {first} and {second}.\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```","thinking":"","partial_json":"","tool_blocks":[],"stop_reason":"max_tokens","start_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"final_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":350,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_